const content = "<p>If these two names are already on your shortlist, you are not hunting for a generic Filipino dating directory. You are trying to decide whether an international, general-purpose site or a Christian-positioned one matches how you want to meet someone, what you can actually do before you pay, and how each company describes safety, billing and exit.</p>\n<p>We write this as FilWest. We are building a project around <a href=\"https://filipinawest.com/\">Filipino-Western relationships</a>, and this is our comparison of public materials, not an independent test, ranking or endorsement. The public homepages, help pages and terms were checked on 24 September 2026. No personal accounts, purchases, messaging, video, safety tools or relationship outcomes were tested or verified. The product descriptions below are the companies\u2019 published statements. If marketing and terms disagree about what you would be buying, pause and ask the company to clarify before you authorise a charge.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-each-site-says-it-is-for\">Who Each Site Says It Is For</h2>\n<p>FilipinoCupid presents itself as an international dating site for Filipino singles and people seeking relationships with them. The <a href=\"https://www.filipinocupid.com/\">FilipinoCupid</a> home page places that international focus within the Cupid Media network of niche dating sites. That positioning matters if you want to search for a Filipino partner without making a Christian identity the premise of the service you choose.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina emphasises Christian values and compatible friendships as a basis for relationships. Its home page presents it as a place for Christian singles seeking faith-based connection, and it describes relationship specialists and a screening process for new applications. That is a different emphasis: shared belief and friendship first, then romance, rather than a general international search.</p>\n<p>Neither public description tells you who will actually reply, how devout a given member is, or whether a profile is current. Positioning tells you the advertised premise, not the person on the other end. If shared Christian practice is non-negotiable, Christian Filipina\u2019s stated focus is the closer fit. If you want Filipino dating without a Christian frame, FilipinoCupid\u2019s positioning matches that wider search.</p>\n<p>Make that distinction concrete before paying. Consider whether you need a partner who shares your church life, whether different beliefs would be acceptable, and how you would discuss faith in a first conversation. A site\u2019s name cannot answer those questions for an individual member. Use the advertised focus as the first cut, then look at how conversation and money actually work.</p>\n<h2 id=\"free-registration-does-not-mean-you-can-talk-freely\">Free Registration Does Not Mean You Can Talk Freely</h2>\n<p>Both sites let you register without paying. The decision is what that free account can send, and what stays locked until someone upgrades.</p>\n<p>FilipinoCupid offers free membership with limited features and charges for access to additional features. <a href=\"https://www.filipinocupid.com/en/general/termsofuse\">FilipinoCupid\u2019s membership terms</a> also describe paid subscriber tiers and coins used for paid extras such as virtual gifts. Before choosing a tier, identify the communication features you need rather than assuming every upgrade includes the same tools. FilipinoCupid states that paid services renew automatically unless you opt out. Before you tap upgrade, read the period, the price on that screen, the currency, and how to turn auto-renewal off in the help section it points to. Auto-renewal is not a minor footnote. It is how the next charge happens if you do nothing.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina\u2019s messaging model is easy to oversimplify, and the public pages do not all describe it the same way. Christian Filipina says two free members can exchange pre-written messages, while a free member can send a custom reply to an upgraded member. That is the access detail that changes behaviour: you can test the waters with stock lines, while replying in your own words depends on the other member\u2019s upgraded status. <a href=\"https://www.christianfilipina.com/faq\">Christian Filipina\u2019s FAQ</a> spells out that free-level and custom-reply distinction, including the point that both people do not need to upgrade for a custom exchange once one of them has.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.christianfilipina.com/terms_of_use.html\">Christian Filipina\u2019s terms</a> put a harder edge on initiation. They say you may register free, and that to use the services to initiate communication with other members you must become a paid member. Read those two documents together rather than picking the softer sentence. Pre-written exchanges and a custom reply to someone who already paid are not the same as unlimited original outreach from a free account. Paid initiation, custom replies and free registration answer different questions. If you need to write your own first message to people who have not paid, check which upgrade permits that and ask for clarification if the offer does not clearly explain it.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina also describes optional site credits, but says messages unlocked with credits cannot contain contact details. Credits buy extra on-site features. They are not a substitute for a full upgrade if the point of paying is to exchange email or a phone number. The same terms say credits have no cash value and purchased credits are non-refundable. If a checkout offers credits instead of, or on top of, a membership, ask whether you are buying conversation inside the site or access that permits exchanging contact details.</p>\n<p>Before budgeting for a month of outreach, check the message limits and price attached to the specific offer. A screenshot or memory of another Cupid Media site does not establish the access you are buying here.</p>\n<h2 id=\"commitment-cancellation-and-refunds-are-separate-switches\">Commitment, Cancellation and Refunds Are Separate Switches</h2>\n<p>Once you pay, the next decision is not just whether you like the site. It is how the contract ends.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina states that a committed payment plan cannot be cancelled to avoid the remaining payments. That is not the same as a subscription you can stop after the current period. If you select a committed series of instalments, you are agreeing to the series, not to a single month you can abandon when the replies disappoint you.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina directs members cancelling auto-renewal after the initial membership period to its online interface or telephone support. A committed first stretch and later auto-renewal can sit on the same membership, so do not treat those as alternative products you pick between. If remaining committed payments are still due, cancelling auto-renewal will not wipe them. Keep confirmation of the cancellation and check which future charges it stops.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina says cancelling membership does not automatically qualify you for a refund. Stopping future charges and recovering money already taken are two requests. The terms also describe cases where using the site during an initial or subsequent upgraded period, including logging in or sending or receiving messages and winks, can remove refund eligibility. Read that before treating a first login as harmless to a possible refund request.</p>\n<p>FilipinoCupid\u2019s refund language is also conditional. <a href=\"https://www.filipinocupid.com/en/general/paymentrefund\">FilipinoCupid\u2019s refund policy</a> describes full refunds in listed situations such as serious technical problems, a request made before any contact with members, and other cases under the terms of use. It also restricts refunds for unused time, while retaining exceptions for qualifying non-use and other cases in those terms. Some US, UK and EU provisions add cancellation rights for qualifying residents. Match the relevant conditions to your residence, start date and use of the service before assuming either that a refund is due or that none is possible.</p>\n<p>Before any membership purchase, establish the amount, currency and billing channel, and whether the plan auto-renews, requires committed payments, or ends after a fixed period. Save the offer and the applicable terms so you have a record of what you accepted. Do not settle an unclear contract by tapping the button that happens to be in front of you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"safety-copy-is-advice-not-a-score\">Safety Copy Is Advice, Not A Score</h2>\n<p>Fit and access still leave the safety question: what each company says it does, and what those measures can tell you about another person.</p>\n<p>Christian Filipina describes profile verification as optional. Its FAQ outlines levels that can include a government-issued ID, and in higher levels additional documents such as a social-security number and a pastor\u2019s letter. Optional means you may see unverified profiles, and a badge is not a criminal record check. The same FAQ states that the company does not conduct criminal background screenings, that identity theft can produce a false profile, and that caution with strangers is still required.</p>\n<p>FilipinoCupid\u2019s terms say the company does not currently undertake routine background checks or routinely verify information provided by members, while reserving the right to investigate and request identification. Its public dating-safety advice recommends keeping early conversations on the platform, watching for money requests or avoidance of calls and meetings, and reporting solicitation.</p>\n<p>These policies describe different checks, not a basis for declaring one site safer. An identity document, a church-affiliation check and a criminal background screening answer different questions. Even a correctly identified person can misrepresent intentions. When assessing a badge, look at what was checked rather than treating the label as approval of everything the member says.</p>\n<p>Pressure to leave the site quickly, disclose private information or send money is a reason to stop and reassess. Never send money to a match, including through wire transfers or gift cards. Meeting someone does not make a financial request safe. If you suspect a scam, save relevant messages and the profile identifier when safe to do so, then use the reporting controls where the conversation happened. If you already sent money, contact your bank or payment provider promptly.</p>\n<p>Keep your own <a href=\"https://filipinawest.com/safety/\">dating safety</a> habits alongside any platform checks. For a first meeting, choose a public place, tell someone you trust where you are going, and retain control of your transport. Those precautions remain useful whichever membership model you choose.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-we-sit-on-this-shortlist\">Where We Sit On This Shortlist</h2>\n<p>Our focus is adult Filipinas and Western partners seeking serious relationships across cultures. That audience focus may interest you, but it is not a current membership alternative to the two services compared here.</p>\n<p>We are preparing a free, invitation-only test of FilWest. Invitations are not open yet. A general free-membership offer and the features available before any future upgrade are not confirmed.</p>\n<p>Our current pricing information says we are not selling a subscription, while our terms still describe app-store subscriptions, auto-renewal and virtual coins and gifts. That is an unresolved conflict in our public information, not evidence that those paid features are available. Ask us to clarify any conflicting access or payment description rather than treating the terms as a released offer. If we offer a paid plan in future, the amount, currency, billing channel, included features and renewal conditions should be clear before you consider paying.</p>\n<p>For now, the available next steps are reading about our project, using our public safety guidance and joining our launch email list for updates. Joining that list does not create a dating account or provide a test invitation. No account, payment or identity documents are needed for launch-list registration, and a launch date has not been announced.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-do-with-the-comparison\">What To Do With The Comparison</h2>\n<p>Choose the advertised focus that matches your search, then check whether its communication model and financial commitment suit how you intend to use the service. FilipinoCupid is the broader international Filipino dating option, with limited free membership and paid features. Christian Filipina puts Christian values and friendship at the centre, with a specific distinction between free pre-written messages, custom replies to upgraded members and paid initiation.</p>\n<p>If shared Christian practice is central to the relationship you want, start with Christian Filipina\u2019s FAQ and terms. Confirm the access you need and whether the offer involves committed instalments before deciding to upgrade. If you prefer a wider international Filipino search, start with FilipinoCupid\u2019s membership terms and refund policy, then check the relevant tier and renewal settings. Neither advertised focus tells you whether an individual member shares your intentions.</p>\n<p>If our Filipino-Western focus interests you, the home page linked above explains our private-test preparation and offers launch updates, not current dating access. Our safety guidance is available now and remains relevant after you pick a site. The practical choice between FilipinoCupid and Christian Filipina is the combination of audience focus, usable communication rights and payment obligations you are comfortable accepting, not a universal winner.</p>";
